1
00:00:00,244 --> 00:00:02,048
Your AI agent nailed the demo.

2
00:00:02,249 --> 00:00:03,404
Will it nail the next eight?

3
00:00:03,812 --> 00:00:05,583
Most leaderboards measure whether it gets it

4
00:00:05,593 --> 00:00:06,442
right once.

5
00:00:06,643 --> 00:00:08,319
But in a business, what matters is

6
00:00:08,329 --> 00:00:09,260
something else:

7
00:00:09,308 --> 00:00:10,805
getting it right every time.

8
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,045
Do the math:

9
00:00:12,128 --> 00:00:13,958
an agent that's right 90% of the

10
00:00:13,968 --> 00:00:15,703
time, if it has to be right

11
00:00:15,713 --> 00:00:17,496
eight times in a row, drops to

12
00:00:17,506 --> 00:00:18,732
43%.

13
00:00:19,132 --> 00:00:20,146
And this isn't theory.

14
00:00:20,335 --> 00:00:22,861
On tau-bench, a customer service test, the

15
00:00:22,871 --> 00:00:25,549
best agents of 2024 succeeded less than

16
00:00:25,559 --> 00:00:27,033
50% of the time…

17
00:00:27,128 --> 00:00:28,875
and eight times in a row, less

18
00:00:28,885 --> 00:00:30,229
than 25%.

19
00:00:30,644 --> 00:00:31,104
Why?

20
00:00:31,305 --> 00:00:33,380
Because an agent doesn't answer a question:

21
00:00:33,545 --> 00:00:35,585
it walks a path of many steps.

22
00:00:35,774 --> 00:00:37,460
A single error brings it all down.

23
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:39,478
So before you buy an agent, don't

24
00:00:39,488 --> 00:00:40,867
ask how often it's right.

25
00:00:41,056 --> 00:00:42,343
Ask how many times in a row

26
00:00:42,353 --> 00:00:43,001
it's right…

27
00:00:43,096 --> 00:00:44,605
and what happens when it fails.

28
00:00:45,016 --> 00:00:46,395
Because a demo is once.

29
00:00:46,596 --> 00:00:47,775
Production is always.

30
00:00:48,188 --> 00:00:49,711
Save it, and share it with someone

31
00:00:49,721 --> 00:00:51,124
who's about to buy an agent.

